# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored — it
# holds machine/environment-specific config (e.g. a LAN IP) and must never
# be committed.

# Section 8's explicit fixture/HTTP source switch (src/repositories/
# create-trail-repository.ts). Leave unset/empty to keep every screen on
# the checked-in fixture trails — that is the default and is safe to ship.
#
# Set it to point at a real trail-pack backend, or at the local dev mock
# server (scripts/mock-trail-server.js) for manual testing:
#   1. node scripts/mock-trail-server.js 4000
#   2. It prints the exact line to use here, e.g.:
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_TRAIL_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.x.x:4000
#   3. Restart Expo with `npx expo start --clear` — .env is only read at
#      startup, not on hot reload.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TRAIL_API_BASE_URL=
